# The 584MB portable toolchain. Re-extract from the w64devkit release rather
# than committing it -- it is a third-party binary distribution, it dwarfs the
# project by four orders of magnitude, and build.ps1 only needs it on PATH.
#
# Excluded by PATH, not by `tools/`: the rest of that directory is source. The
# headless tests and the model/map editors under tools/*.c are as much a part
# of this project as src/ is, and a blanket `tools/` rule silently drops them.
tools/w64devkit/

# Build output. Everything here is regenerated by build.ps1.
build/
*.exe
*.o

# NOT `*.map`, which used to be here. It was for the linker's game.map, and
# `build/` above already covers that -- build.ps1 writes it nowhere else. What
# it also did, from the moment levels became .map files, was swallow every one
# of them: assets/maps/*.map is the SOURCE form of a level, written by
# TrenchBroom and read by src/brush.c, and `git status` showed nothing at all.
#
# Same failure the note above `tools/w64devkit/` describes: a blanket pattern
# that silently drops source. A level that is never committed is a level that
# exists on one machine.
#
# `*.map`이 여기 있었는데 제거했습니다. 링커의 game.map을 위한 규칙이었고, 위의 `build/`가
# 이미 그것을 덮습니다. build.ps1은 그 파일을 다른 곳에 쓰지 않습니다. 레벨이 .map 파일이 된
# 순간부터 이 규칙이 한 일은 그 레벨들을 전부 삼키는 것이었습니다. assets/maps/*.map은 레벨의
# *원본* 형태이며 TrenchBroom이 쓰고 src/brush.c가 읽는데, `git status`에는 아무것도 나타나지
# 않았습니다. 위의 `tools/w64devkit/` 설명이 말하는 것과 같은 실패입니다. 소스를 조용히
# 떨어뜨리는 포괄 패턴입니다. 결코 커밋되지 않는 레벨은 한 대의 기계에만 존재하는 레벨입니다.

# Baked assets: regenerated from assets/*.txt by bake.ps1 on every build, so
# committing it would mean a file that conflicts on every branch and that no
# human ever reads.
src/gen_assets.h

# Freedoom lumps downloaded by assets/sprites/import-freedoom.py. Upstream art
# in its original form: the PNGs the importer produces from it ARE committed,
# so nothing here is needed to build, and re-downloading is one command.
assets/sprites/.freedoom-cache/

# A contact sheet the importer writes with --preview, for looking at the
# conversion. Regenerated on demand and never read by the build.
assets/sprites/_preview.png

# Freedoom lumps downloaded by assets/sounds/import-freedoom.py, at their
# original rates. The 11025Hz WAVs the importer writes from them ARE committed,
# so nothing here is needed to build.
assets/sounds/.freedoom-cache/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vs/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Freedoom wall patches downloaded by assets/sprites/import-walls.py. Same
# reasoning as the two caches above: upstream art at its original size, kept
# only so a re-run does not re-fetch. What the project carries is the converted
# 128x128 PNGs beside it, which ARE committed.
assets/sprites/.freedoom-walls/

# Python leaves this behind when a tool imports another tool -- sprtest's
# verification does that to reuse the importer's PNG reader rather than write a
# second one.
__pycache__/

# tools\sprdump writes this beside the working directory, which is the repo
# root when build.ps1 launches a tool. It is a raw dump of the sprite atlas for
# looking at, regenerated on demand, and it is 2MB of a file nobody reads
# twice. It came within one commit of being committed.
# tools\sprdump가 작업 디렉터리 옆에 씁니다. build.ps1이 도구를 실행할 때 그곳은 저장소
# 루트입니다. 스프라이트 아틀라스를 눈으로 보기 위한 원본 덤프이며, 필요할 때 다시 만들어지고,
# 아무도 두 번 읽지 않는 2MB짜리 파일입니다. 커밋될 뻔했습니다.
sprites.ppm

# TrenchBroom's autosaves. The editor writes `<map>.N.map` beside the map it is
# editing, and it keeps writing them for maps that have since left the tree --
# 1.7MB of lqdm1 and spire sat here untracked, both recoverable from history and
# neither shippable. `git status` listed them, which means one `git add -A`
# would have put editor scratch into a repository whose whole discipline is a
# 1.44MB budget.
#
# TrenchBroom의 자동 저장입니다. 편집기는 편집 중인 맵 곁에 `<맵>.N.map`을 쓰며, 그 뒤로 트리를
# 떠난 맵에 대해서도 계속 씁니다. lqdm1과 spire의 1.7MB가 추적되지 않은 채 있었고, 둘 다 이력에서
# 복구 가능하며 어느 쪽도 출하되지 않습니다. `git status`가 그것들을 나열했으니, `git add -A` 한
# 번이면 1.44MB 예산이 규율의 전부인 저장소에 편집기의 임시 파일이 들어갔을 것입니다.
assets/maps/autosave/

# Python bytecode from the asset importers. Regenerated on every run.
# 에셋 임포터가 남기는 파이썬 바이트코드입니다. 실행할 때마다 다시 만들어집니다.
__pycache__/
